-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Light to moderate rain showers will continue across the southwest\nmountains through the morning, with scattered showers and\npossible thunderstorms, developing across the region through the\nafternoon. Rain, locally heavy associated with the afternoon\nshowers and thunderstorms, will exacerbate ongoing flooding\nissues across the eastern San Juan mountains and Upper Rio Grande\nvalley.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231709 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1109 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains in effect through this afternoon for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Rainfall starting to diminish across the higher terrain through this morning, then ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:58:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 231758 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1158 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241800- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB